{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfiK5rtbzS87YzkjMQZyj", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "```\nTable 3 reports the estimates. Identity disclosure carries a coefficient of 0.18 (SE = 0.04) in column 2, and it holds at 0.15 (SE = 0.05) in column 3 once we add product fixed effects. Column 4 adds the interaction with reviewer tenure, which comes in at 0.09 (SE = 0.03). Star rating remains a strong predictor throughout, at 0.42 (SE = 0.02) in every specification. Across the columns, R-squared rises from 0.31 to 0.47. All coefficients are significant at the 1% level except the interaction, which is significant at the 5% level.\n```\n\nI kept every number and the order of results. I made three changes:\n- Each estimate now leads its sentence, with the specification as the frame around it.\n- Verbs like \"holds\" and \"remains\" carry the contrast between columns.\n- Star rating is positioned as the stable benchmark against which the identity results read.\n\nI didn't add interpretation, such as calling the effect large or explaining the fixed-effects result, since that would go beyond your claims. If you'd like the paragraph to close on the thesis, I can add a sentence tying the results back to identity, but you'd need to confirm the claim."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1657, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1391, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1657}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "67a85a5c-5528-50ca-a038-89c6a50acf16", "uuid": "e7b51eb7-03a0-46c1-a8db-928981816c5f", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T02:37:03.291Z", "request_id": "req_011CfiK5rfTf1wSVZAtYPWXC"}
